<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="policy-page">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="policy-header">
      <p class="policy-brand">NovBank</p>
      <h1 class="policy-title">Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="policy-date">Last updated: January 1, 2025</p>
    </div>

    <div class="policy-body">

      <div class="policy-section">
        <h2>1. What Are Cookies</h2>
        <p>Cookies are small text files that are placed on your device when you visit a website. They are widely used to make websites work more efficiently, provide security features and give website owners information about how their site is being used. Cookies can be session cookies which expire when you close your browser, or persistent cookies which remain on your device for a set period.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-section">
        <h2>2. How NovBank Uses Cookies</h2>
        <p>NovBank uses a minimal and privacy-focused approach to cookies. We only use cookies that are strictly necessary for the platform to function securely. We do not use advertising cookies, marketing cookies or third-party tracking cookies of any kind.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-section">
        <h2>3. Cookies We Use</h2>
        <p>The following cookies are used on the NovBank platform:</p>
        <div class="cookie-table-wrap">
          <table class="cookie-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Cookie Name</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Duration</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>connect.sid</code></td>
                <td>Essential</td>
                <td>Maintains your login session and keeps you authenticated while using the platform. Without this cookie you would need to log in on every page.</td>
                <td>24 hours</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>pinVerified</code></td>
                <td>Essential</td>
                <td>Stores whether you have successfully entered your transaction PIN during your current session. This prevents you from having to re-enter your PIN on every page.</td>
                <td>Session</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>flash</code></td>
                <td>Essential</td>
                <td>Temporarily stores notification messages such as success or error alerts so they can be displayed to you after a page redirect.</td>
                <td>Session</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-section">
        <h2>4. Essential Cookies</h2>
        <p>All cookies used by NovBank are classified as essential or strictly necessary cookies. These cookies are required for the platform to function properly and to maintain the security of your account and session. As they are essential to the service, they cannot be disabled while you are using NovBank.</p>
        <p>Under GDPR and the ePrivacy Directive, strictly necessary cookies do not require your consent as they are essential for the provision of a service you have explicitly requested.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-section">
        <h2>5. Cookies We Do Not Use</h2>
        <p>NovBank does not use the following types of cookies:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Advertising cookies:</strong> We do not use cookies to show you targeted advertisements</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics cookies:</strong> We do not use third-party analytics tools such as Google Analytics that track your behaviour across websites</li>
          <li><strong>Social media cookies:</strong> We do not embed social media buttons or widgets that set cookies</li>
          <li><strong>Marketing cookies:</strong> We do not track your browsing habits for marketing purposes</li>
          <li><strong>Third-party tracking cookies:</strong> We do not allow third parties to place cookies on our platform for tracking purposes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-section">
        <h2>6. Managing Cookies</h2>
        <p>You can control and manage cookies through your browser settings. Most browsers allow you to refuse or delete cookies. However, please note that disabling essential cookies will prevent you from logging in and using the NovBank platform as intended.</p>
        <p>Here are links to cookie management instructions for common browsers:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Google Chrome: Settings > Privacy and Security > Cookies</li>
          <li>Mozilla Firefox: Options > Privacy and Security > Cookies</li>
          <li>Apple Safari: Preferences > Privacy > Cookies</li>
          <li>Microsoft Edge: Settings > Privacy, Search and Services > Cookies</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-section">
        <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or applicable regulations. The date at the top of this page indicates when the policy was last revised. Continued use of the NovBank platform following any changes constitutes your acceptance of the updated policy.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>